queen elizabeth ii was britain's longest  reigning monarch a popular and  stabilizing force who ruled for over 70  years  during her reign she became a cultural  and political icon the subject of  hollywood films  and tv shows the crown must win  as well as a host to an array of global  leaders  but others in the royal family are not  as popular including her successor king  charles iii in a recent poll 32 of the  british public said he wouldn't make a  good king  in recent years some members have also  been embroiled in scandals and royal  rifts have spilled into the public eye  so as the country mourns the queen the  transition to a pneumonic is a delicate  one as charles and the rest of the  family have to step up to fill the void  she leaves and make their own mark  here's how it will work  first consider that the queen is deeply  embedded in almost every aspect of  britain's everyday life  [Applause]  the british national anthem has been  sung in honour of the queen  her image is emblazoned on cash and  coins and on postage  and every uk passport is issued in the  queen's name  so as king charles ascends to the throne  all of these items will need to be  updated a process that is expected to  take years and could cost billions  culturally it will be a big change for  the uk where most people were born under  the queen's reign  [Music]  and while those changes can happen  gradually the royals face the immediate  challenges of preparing for the queen's  funeral and subsequent coronation of  king charles  like his mother and other british  monarchs for the past 900 years king  charles is expected to have his  coronation service at westminster abbey  but even as he continues those  long-standing traditions the monarch is  expected to make some key changes  aides say he wants to slim down and  lower the cost of the monarchy as an  institution while remaining very active  in britain's national life  part of that will be determined by where  charles will live or spend most of his  time the british royal family has many  estates including balmoral in scotland  where the queen died and sandringham  where the family traditionally spends  christmas  charles is widely expected to move into  buckingham palace the administrative  headquarters of the monarchy whereas in  recent years the queen spent much of her  time at windsor castle outside of london  one of the hardest tasks for charles  will be to establish his moral authority  he takes over in the wake of family  rifts from prince harry leaving his  royal duties to prince andrew's  friendship with convicted sex offender  jeffrey epstein  in the past the king's own personal life  has been the subject of interest for the  nation's tabloids particularly in the  1990s following his separation from lady  diana and remarriage to camilla  parker-bowles who will now become queen  consort  his son and heir to the throne william  is more popular than his father  overall the public perception of the  monarchy has changed in 2012 more than  70 percent of british respondents in a  survey said they supported the royals  ten years later that number has dropped  by 11 points and one in five people  questioned if the uk should move to have  an elected head of state like a  president  that's a choice many countries that used  to be part of the commonwealth have  already made barbados was the latest  country to remove the queen as head of  state in 2021  during a visit to the caribbean island  charles didn't shy away from addressing  the family's colonial history from the  darkest days  of our past  and the appalling atrocity of slavery  which forever stains our history  one key difference between charles and  his mother while the queen steered clear  of political debates charles has often  called for change in action on issues  such as climate change  as all the  horrors of even a two-degree warmer  world bite  and bite they will  royal aids says king charles will step  back from campaigning and overall they  expect his popularity to rise as people  embrace him as a monarch as he becomes  king at 73 charles iii has had decades  to prepare and study for this role  unlike his mother who was in her 20s  when she became queen  still he faces a delicate task as he  shapes the future of the british  monarchy
 

